{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly","id":1512416,"title":"Can a super-trained human defeat a Garou or elder vampire barehandedly?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-23T02:20:18-07:00","id":1512416,"title":"Can a super-trained human defeat a Garou or elder vampire barehandedly?","content":"A little homebrew: a mortal character ( no ghoul, no sorcery, no infernal investments ) trained to the human limit in several martial arts ( Combat Styles from Armory Reloaded, transposed in the Old World of Darkness ruleset ).<br /> If I remember well there was a rule for extra use of Willpower in the book Mirrors. I've to research it.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, the question is: without going into the blatantly supernatural, can the strongest human take on a truly powerful supernatural being?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> So far:<br /> <br /> Strength ( heavy blows ) 5<br /> Dexterity ( close combat ) 5<br /> <br /> Dodge ( one-on-one ) 5<br /> Brawl ( boxing ) 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> * Ability aptitude - dodge<br /> * Ability aptitude - brawl<br /> * Berserker ( V20 Black Hand )<br /> <br /> Flaws:<br /> * Stress Atavism ( Guide to the Technocracy )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-23-2023, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T02:36:49-07:00","id":1512419,"title":"","content":"In a one-on-one hand to hand fight? Not really. Humans beat supernaturals by fighting smart... trying to fight things in close combat that can soak your attacks, and you can't soak theirs, on top of whatever supernatural powers they have, is suicidal. Assuming said supernatural doesn't just walk away from the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T03:43:53-07:00","id":1512421,"title":"","content":"Werewolf and eldar is going to shred you. Bring silver rounds for the and show up at 1pm for the elder <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T03:53:18-07:00","id":1512422,"title":"","content":"Well, let's at least make a try!<br /> <br /> I would start with maximizing Dodge: if you can't soak, the second best is to not get hit at all.<br /> So, Dexterity 5 with a specialization ( &quot;hand-to-hand combat&quot; ) and Dodge 5 with a specialization ( &quot;one-on-one duel&quot; ). We have 12 dices for dodging, which means an average of 6 successes.<br /> Then, there is Merit &quot;Ability Aptitude&quot; ( <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Players_Guide_to_High_Clans\" target=\"_blank\">Players Guide to High Clans</a>\u200b ), if the DM doesn't veto it for a combat ability like Dodge... but since we're putting a mortal human against a werewolf, let's assume a bit of generosity. With the Dodge difficulty reduced to 4, we'll have something aroung 8 successes for our dodging attempts.<br /> <br /> It's good , the first attack from the beast is almost automatically eluded, problem is these supernaturals have the bad habit of attacking more than once every turn...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T04:04:21-07:00","id":1512423,"title":"","content":"You might be able to take down a less experiences werewolf or vampire who is not really much of a fighter, but as soon as they are somewhat decent at fighting and have multiple actions through celerity or rage you a pretty much screwed (how much depends on what edition and splat you are using).<br /> <br /> Werewolfs can also regenerate damage and vampires can heal with blood, and only take half damage from bashing damage.<br /> <br /> So unless you are fighting a really weak one you need for werewolf probaly a silver weapon, and for a Vampire something that does at least lethal damage (agg would be better of course).<br /> <br /> Elder Vampires can also have Attributes and Abilities above 5 so that they could even take you without using their other powers.<br /> <br /> Even if I can't really rule out that there are some Elder Vampires with stats so terrible that they could actually get their ass kicked my a mortal martial artist, a lot some of the official NPCs are kind of poorly build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 05-23-2023, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T04:48:12-07:00","id":1512425,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5199\" data-vbnamecard=\"5199\">Aahz</a>.<br /> <br /> So, the second problem is dealing enough damage. And the third is that those supernatural powerhouses have multiple actions every round ( Celerity and Rage )<br /> Let's see.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the basics: Strength 5 with specialization (&quot;heavy blows&quot; ) plus Brawl 5 with specialization ( boxing, karate, whatever ) and Ability Aptitude - Brawl. This gives us a base of 12 attack dice with a difficulty of 4, so roughly 8 successes. Problem is, it's bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Then, there's this Merit/Flaw from Guide to the Technocracy called &quot;Stress Atavism&quot;. It's common between cyborgs and genetical soldiers but it doesn't say it can't be taken by a common human.<br /> For most characters it's something innate but I think that certain ecstatic pratices can allow a warrior to develope a similar &quot;murderous istinct&quot; by training and mental conditioning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stress Atavism (3 pt Flaw) Despite the ice-cold Technocrat stereotype, you go ballistic at any provocation. You revert to an animalistic state of mind, diving into fight-or-flight instincts. The good points: You become extremely strong and nearly invulnerable to pain. The bad points: You attack everything in your vicinity, forgetting small details like friendships, tactics or innocent bystanders. While this heedless mania makes you good in a fight, your comrades tend to wind you up and run. A common Flaw among genetically engineered constructs and cybernetically enhanced soldiers, Stress Atavism surges up during combat or other high-stress situations. If the Storyteller asks you to make a Willpower roll (difficulty 8) and you fail, the madness overcomes you. In your atavistic state, add two dice to your Strength, one die to your Stamina and three &quot;Bruised&quot; health levels. You also go completely apeshit, firing all weapons at full-auto until the magazines empty, then lashing out with hands, feet and anything else that seems convenient. Once you go atavistic, you fight until one of two things happens: either you are rendered helpless, or everyone else in the area is. Naturally, Control considers you an extraordinarily loose cannon. There's a termination order waiting for the day you outlive your usefulness....\u200b<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>So, we have an ( uncontrollable ) fighting frenzy that can somewhat make up for the Rage of a Garou. +2 Strength, +1 Stamina, +3 bruised health levels and immunity to pain.<br /> We are on something but it's still not enough...<br /> <br /> <br /> Question: the Merit &quot;Too Tough to Die&quot; allows a character who's normally unable to soak lethal damage with Stamina to do so.<br /> But since mortals do not take aggravated damage, would that merit allow a human to soak damage from werewolf bite / claws?<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the suggestion <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5199\" data-vbnamecard=\"5199\">Aahz</a> . So, with Berserk we have 14 attack dices ( 5 Strength + 5 Brawl + 2 specializations + 2 Stress Atavism ) at difficulty 6-3 ( Berserk ) -2 ( Ability Aptitude ): 2 ( minimum difficulty ).<br /> An average of 12-13 successess... but still bashing damage, for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-23-2023, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T05:26:57-07:00","id":1512430,"title":"","content":"You could also take the Berserker Merit from the V20 Black Hand Book, that iirc reduced the difficulty of all combat roles (except dodge) by -3 and gives you pain immunity.<br /> <br /> But with just Bashing Damage you are simply not achieving much against a real power house. The ceiling for supernaturals is just much higher. Werewolfs and Elder vampires can when you really go for it probably pile more additional dice (and auto success) on their soak roles (and their block/parry/doge roles) than you can on you attack and damage.<br /> <br /> But without having a more clear measure of how powerfull the being is you want to fight it is really impossible to say if hat could ever work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T05:45:14-07:00","id":1512433,"title":"","content":"If you begin the fight with surprise and target the head, yeah. You can probably crack that open before retaliation. Vampires and werewolves can be stunned and can underestimate threats. <br /> <br /> But honestly someone with 5/5/X and 5 brawl is less realistic in the WoD than someone with a power. <i>Batman</i> is less believable than a good chunk of superpowered heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:12:11-07:00","id":1512439,"title":"","content":"Remember, with a Garou it isn't just that you're fighting someone bigger, stronger, with natural weapons they have rage which means multiple actions at no penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:29:15-07:00","id":1512443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512430#post1512430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>But without having a more clear measure of how powerfull the being is you want to fight it is really impossible to say if hat could ever work</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to do something like this:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" data-thumb-url=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a></div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Dfm9x9T/15-Copia-2-Copia.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" target=\"_blank\"> 15-Copia-2-Copia hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image 15-Copia-2-Copia hosted on ImgBB </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/5Wxx7bf/15-Copia.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW\" target=\"_blank\"> 15-Copia hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image 15-Copia hosted on ImgBB </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or this ( probably that's a Metis ):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Wc4Wk60/15-Copia-2.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY\" target=\"_blank\"> 15-Copia-2 hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image 15-Copia-2 hosted on ImgBB </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> These images come from World of Darkness - Armory Reloaded.<br /> <br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Stat speaking, I mean fighting a combat oriented but inexperienced Garou ( a starting character Garou built for combat ) or an elder of comparable fighting prowess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T07:29:16-07:00","id":1512453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512443#post1512443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stat speaking, I mean fighting a combat oriented but inexperienced Garou ( a starting character Garou built for combat ) or an elder of comparable fighting prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok that might be potenatlly doable if that Garou or Vampire isn't to min maxed, but it would really come down to what rules you are using. Since the rules for splitting actions can differ a lot beween differnt books. In some cases you have to split you lowest involved dice pool between all actions, in some cases you get just a dice penalty that increases the number of actions.<br /> <br /> And at least the Rules for Celerity were also differ from edition to edition. (Not sure about Rage)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T08:40:54-07:00","id":1512457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512443#post1512443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to do something like this:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" data-thumb-url=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Dfm9x9T/15-Copia-2-Copia.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" target=\"_blank\"> 15-Copia-2-Copia hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/Xx67h7M </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image 15-Copia-2-Copia hosted on ImgBB </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/5Wxx7bf/15-Copia.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW\" target=\"_blank\"> 15-Copia hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/tMPPdVW </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image 15-Copia hosted on ImgBB </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or this ( probably that's a Metis ):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Wc4Wk60/15-Copia-2.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY\" target=\"_blank\"> 15-Copia-2 hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/xMtS1DY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image 15-Copia-2 hosted on ImgBB </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> These images come from World of Darkness - Armory Reloaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does one come to the conclusion that a werewolf is Crinos-born in a setting where there is no Crinos, but Gauru, and there are none born in that form because they ripped off the Mokole's scary ghost babies to make werewolf on werewolf action even worse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - - -<br /> <br /> Stat speaking, I mean fighting a combat oriented but inexperienced Garou ( a starting character Garou built for combat ) or an elder of comparable fighting prowess. </div> </div> </div>So, a character that can have the same attack and defense dice pools in human form, but with the ability to change forms who can also make you fall down with the slightest touch or dive into a fire knowing that it'll only bruise them? Or they can jump over 60 feet, or snap their fingers and set you on fire?<br /> <br /> How, exactly, do you <i>think</i> that's going to turn out? To only slightly misquote one of the best James Bond opening themes, if you thought that you won, you never saw them change the game that you were playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-27-2023, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T09:13:22-07:00","id":1512462,"title":"","content":"One on one? I'd say no as powerful vampires &amp; werewolves got a major edge with there supernatural abilities and smart hunters know this and won't fight that way. There going to be intelligent and choose there own moments to strike that favor them and use specialized gear to help even the odds.<br /> <br /> I.E. I wouldn't fight Theo Bell in a close quarters as his physical disciplines are quite strong and I would spend a fair amount of time learning his activities and skills and wait until he is asleep in whatever place he is holed up and hope that our recon was enough to reduce risks as much as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T14:20:32-07:00","id":1512489,"title":"","content":"I think this needs to pump the brakes a bit.<br /> <br /> What edition(s) are fair game? If we're just picking and choosing shit from all the books (including using 2e Merits with X20 base mechanics that have different versions of those Merits) and so on, it's just going to be a mess that generates no useful answers.<br /> <br /> Like the whole Dex 5/Brawl 5 with applicable specialty in both... in no edition or iteration of the cWoD does that result in a dice-pool of 12 with a 0.5 average success rate (before Merits and all). We'd have to be mixing and matching at least three edition's definitions of things for that to happen.<br /> <br /> And that's going to swing the other way to. Disciplines like Celerity, Potence, and Fortitude? Are we using the strongest, the weakest, or a specific editions iteration of them? Because that's going to matter a lot. Are we using 1e Werewolf's rules that have a glitch in them that make them impossible to actually defeat as long as they've taken 1 bashing damage?<br /> <br /> If we want to be serious about this, we have to set clear ground rules or it's meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T15:56:51-07:00","id":1512500,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Dominate and telling a mortal to turn around works in just about every edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T16:25:34-07:00","id":1512502,"title":"","content":"While true, our maximized human is probably going to be given Willpower 10. And edition does matter because some editions set core Dominate powers at permanent Willpower and other temporary Willpower (and botching Dominate tends to immunize targets). So in some editions Dominate isn't really a great option to just ignore the human (compared to, say, Protean 5) at all, and others you just need to exhaust the human a bit before ordering them to get lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T22:17:49-07:00","id":1512543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512500#post1512500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Dominate and telling a mortal to turn around works in just about every edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to restrict a discussion like this anyway purely to physical combat and the respective powers (so in case of Vampires for example to the three physical disciplines and certain powers for discipines like Protean, Serpentis and Vicissitude), since you have probably in editions and splats of the game so mind control or debuff powers or something else that could easily take out an opponent without a fight (or weaken him so much that he doesn't really have chance) if he has not the right power or merit to counter it.<br /> <br /> And likely to some sort of arena fight scenario.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T06:53:53-07:00","id":1512568,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about a brutal fist-to-claw scenario. I guess that a strong elder vampire would feel humiliated if he had to resort to Dominate a single unarmed human who is facing him in a one-to-one duel. And a werewolf... I guess would die of shame if he don't takes the challenge.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to counter Dominate there's the 3 point merit Iron Will:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">3 </span></span><span style=\"font-family:vampire\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Iron Will</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">When you are determined and your mind is set, nothing can thwart you from your goals. When you are affected by a </span></span><a href=\"http://bajor_bhavael.tripod.com/wod/disciplines/dominate.html\" target=\"_blank\">Dominate</a><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> power, you may spend a point of Willpower to shake off the effects. In additon, you receive three extra dice to resist the effects of any mind-altering magic, spell or </span></span><a href=\"http://bajor_bhavael.tripod.com/wod/disciplines/thaumaturgy.html\" target=\"_blank\">Thaumaturgy</a><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> path. This Merit does not affect </span></span><a href=\"http://bajor_bhavael.tripod.com/wod/disciplines/presence.html\" target=\"_blank\">Presence</a><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> or other powers dealing with the emotions.</span></span>\u200b </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I guess there is no official rule conversion for Fighting Style merits?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> I found this on Hunters Hunted<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:vampire\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Fist of God </span></span><i>(Hunters)</i><br /> You can deliver blows to Kindred that cause aggravated damage. You should work with the Storyteller to come up with the reasons why. <i><b>Maybe you spent long years in a dojo, refining your martial arts chi by punching bowls of tightly-packed sand until your fists were raw, scintillating chi energy. </b></i>Or your vision quest led to the Cave of the Wolf, where a half-man/haif-wolf put claws on your hands to be used in the battle against your enemy. One option is that you need a weapon such as a sword or bullet to use this power. The damage done is as much as your fist (or whatever weapon it is defined as) normally does, but is considered to be aggravated against Kindred. Only mortals with a Humanity of 7 or higher may purchase this Merit, although many supernatural hunters possess it as a racial or magical ability for instance, the claws of werewolves.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div><i>It is</i> blatantly supernatural, but it's also something that - according to the text - can be developed by training rather than being an innate faculty or a magical modification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-24-2023, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:20:11-07:00","id":1512576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512568#post1512568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about a brutal fist-to-claw scenario. I guess that a strong elder vampire would feel humiliated if he had to resort to Dominate a single unarmed human who is facing him in a one-to-one duel. And a werewolf... I guess would die of shame if he don't takes the challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's fine to restrict the scenario to a straight hand-to-hand fight because that's the concept you want to explore. But the idea that either supernatural is more likely than not to resort to a &quot;fair fight&quot; over pride, honour, etc., is a bit dubious. In particular, a vampire that has spent time building up their skills with Dominate is probably not going to be one who views using it as a blow to their pride; they're going to be the ones that see it as a blatant demonstration of their superiority, and they're at least as likely to revel in that rather than turn their nose up at it, IMO.<br /> <br /> I think you make a better case for the Garou, as warrior pride tends to be a big deal for them. But even that is going to come with caveats; a Bone Gnawer is a lot less likely to walk into an unfavourable scenario and try and power through it out of hubris than a member of the Get. Garou of any kind are also more likely to have some kind of combat ability, because their entire society exists on a war footing, whereas plenty of vampires are pretty happy to mostly avoid trouble whenever possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512568#post1512568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found this on Hunters Hunted<br /> <br /> ~ ~<br /> <br /> <i>It is</i> blatantly supernatural, but it's also something that - according to the text - can be developed by training rather than being an innate faculty or a magical modification.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ultimately your scenario, and I feel like this Merit might be interesting to explore as an edge case. But I think that, if you allow this, then you ought to allow hedge magic as well. AFAIK linear sorcery is something developed purely through education and training as well. While not everyone has it in them to dedicate themselves and become a full-on Sorcerer, in theory anyone can learn a few dots in a hedge magic Path if they choose, IIRC.<br /> <br /> This doesn't seem like something that any random can pick up by just punching trees for ten years. You need some kind of special instruction if it isn't being granted by some other explicitly supernatural source. That just doesn't seem very different from picking up some minor magical tricks. It may be that allowing hedge magic is what makes the most sense to you, since people using sorcery are still explicitly human and aren't restricted by special bloodlines or spiritual connections. (maybe you did already give sorcery a pass and I missed it; sorry if that's the case!)<br /> <br /> But if you really are looking for Charles Atlas vs. the Supernatural, then I don't think this Merit applies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:17:22-07:00","id":1512589,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's too supernatural.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> The only way to attack multiple times and inflict lethal damage barehandedly, for a Charles Atlas, as far as I know is to take a merit from the New World of Darkness rules.<br /> With Fighting Style - kung fu ( 5 ) you can both launch 4 attacks for round with relatively low penalities and inflict lethal damage by spending 1 Willpower per round.<br /> But it would require to convert fighting style merits from the New to the Old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:43:39-07:00","id":1512593,"title":"","content":"If you want to explore all the available options from all splats, regardless of whom it is actually aimed at, and always rule their allowance in favor of the mortal, it is just easier to decide that yes, it is certainly possible. At that stage you have already determined it is a possibility and it will become one.<br /> <br /> Could they without absurdities? Perhaps, but unlikely. <br /> Animalism can sap the fighting will of anyone. It's quite nasty against mortals.<br /> Auspex will warn the elder in advance, allowing them to prepare or retreat. A physical threat being the easiest to detect.<br /> Celerity will make odds uneven or allow for escapes.<br /> Dominate will end the fight before it starts.<br /> Fortitude will allow the elder to loose a roll. It is probably the poorest choice, unless at 6+, where it might just break the poor mortal.<br /> Obfuscate can end any fight or make it impossible in the first place.<br /> Potence... While Celerity gets a lot of credit for power, Potence is in my opinion the real killer, in particular using combat manouvers relying on strength. Grapple with high Potence versus no Potence is the most efficient physical way to end a fight. <br /> Presence have multiple ways of just ending or preventing fights. It can be fought off using willpower, but botching willpower rolls is nasty and supply will run out quickly, in particular since there are so many of them that can be applied.<br /> <br /> Now, an Elder does not have all of these, but even with 10 dots divided among them there are multiple ways to stop or outright win a fight. Add clan-specific disciplines, in particular powers from Thaumaturgy and Necromancy that will kill a mortal by simply succeeding (which a single expenditure of willpower ensures), it quickly gets one sided.<br /> Then add low generation and a large amount of blood, which may make an attribute match the entire dice pool of a mortal.<br /> The vampire fangs are also versatile, with Potence, the bite is a death sentence to anything but the most resilient creatures, or it could just impose the kiss, which knock outs mortal resistance without a pass, and even has a chance to do the same to supernatural. And this is built in.<br /> <br /> Could a mortal have a streak of good luck and win? Yes. But it is not likely. How unlikely depends on the Elder.<br /> A mortal this well trained would be wasted trying to go head-to-head, but very dangerous actually exploiting the glaring weaknesses of the supernatural, both physical and social. Daytime and the Masquerade against Kindred are much more potent weapons.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> In Revised, though, the most efficient way to beat something head-to-head is by Retainers 5. This is simply due to the funky multiple combatants rule that increases difficulty by 1 for each opponent attacking the same target, quickly putting mostly everything at difficulty 10, at which point size of dice pools no longer matter (just watch out for those automatic Potence successes!). But I supposed Obtenebroken has the same built in feature. Unsure if this carried over to V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T11:10:09-07:00","id":1512604,"title":"","content":"I don't get the insistence on no magic when anyone with that level of strength has a very high chance of being on steroids. Like, It's possible not to, but unlikely.<br /> <br /> 2 hours a day, three days a week, training strength. The rest is very important for gaining strength and/or mass. Steroids would help recovery times.<br /> Somehow also having the time to train and maintain fighting skills. You could probably do some light movement during recovery times but sparring would be eh.<br /> Not getting injured.<br /> <br /> having the knowledge or mentor to train you optimally, yet somehow coming to the conclusion that not using a weapon would ever be a good idea.<br /> <br /> For a non practitioner, it seems really cool to not use a weapon, but in reality, unless your only options are incredibly unwieldy, <i>anything</i> is an advantage. I trained twice a week for a decade learning different styles of kickboxing, while my weapon experience amounts to trying out drills I saw from a few sabre youtube tutorials: I'd still chose a weapon. and even in the less sport-centric practices there's nothing you could really do that wouldn't be better with a weapon. Even if I thought I could kill someone with a kick, I'd feel better with a stick or a rock or a key or something in my hand. It's certainly easier to swing a club than land a kick. Brawl is either for scuffles or a last resort, both put the human at an extreme disadvantage to the supernatural. That said, while some parts of swinging weapons around can seem counterintuitive for someone experienced with brawl, a lot of it does carry over. Footwork for example. With some smaller weapons virtually nothing changes and I'd be happy to let characters use their brawl skill with smaller melee weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-24-2023, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T11:58:24-07:00","id":1512609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512568#post1512568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about a brutal fist-to-claw scenario. I guess that a strong elder vampire would feel humiliated if he had to resort to Dominate a single unarmed human who is facing him in a one-to-one duel. And a werewolf... I guess would die of shame if he don't takes the challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're not of the people, you have no honor or standing among them. Their culture only encourages challenges from a certain small segment of their own society. If a human stands up and tries this, when the Garou are in Crinos? The Garou is going to assume that they're something way more resilient than they actually are - a combat fomor, for example - and just kill them. They'd still be non-person without the right to challenge, in any case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, to counter Dominate there's the 3 point merit Iron Will: </div> </div> </div>Its effects have steadily made their way into &quot;more of a suggestion than a hard defense&quot; over the years. V20 has a paragraph about how elder levels of a Discipline can overwhelm it, with the bonus attentuating for every dot of the power past 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess there is no official rule conversion for Fighting Style merits?<br /> - - - </div> </div> </div>Get yourself a copy of WoD: Combat or Demon Hunter X. I'd even allow the old Street Fighter rpg, given the circumstances. At any rate, there are combat maneuvers in those books that can multi-attack - usually only two or three attacks, at little to no penalty, but with a typically steep Willpower expenditure. You'll probably break your hands punching the occult being you're fighting, though, especially if, say, you're up against a werebeast that's trained in Maka Wara. And if you're fighting Rokea trained in this way, then your hands are probably broken <i>and also</i> horribly cut!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I found this on Hunters Hunted<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>It is</i> blatantly supernatural, but it's also something that - according to the text - can be developed by training rather than being an innate faculty or a magical modification. </div> </div> </div>Per Hunter's Hunted 2, that's been relegated to being a religious-based merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T13:36:41-07:00","id":1512624,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I was thinking about one of those super-fanatic martial artists from quasi-realistic martial arts mangas like Shamo or Tough.<br /> <br /> I fully agree that humans should use weapons instead of fists when facing lions, bears, tigers or supernaturals. Also, humans hunting supernaturals should always seek for terrain advantages and strength in number.<br /> This is just an extreme hypothetical scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T14:11:36-07:00","id":1512631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512624#post1512624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I was thinking about one of those super-fanatic martial artists from quasi-realistic martial arts mangas like Shamo or Tough.</div> </div> </div> </div>way I could see this working in WoD is something like faith, unknowing possession, or accidental magic(k) <br /> <br /> You train real hard, awaken as a mage, not really realize you're doing magic, accidentally do awesome feats. something something yeah yeah... <br /> There's a hunter merit that gives fists aggravated damage, because faith in fists is wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T15:00:49-07:00","id":1512638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512568#post1512568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about a brutal fist-to-claw scenario. I guess that a strong elder vampire would feel humiliated if he had to resort to Dominate a single unarmed human who is facing him in a one-to-one duel. And a werewolf... I guess would die of shame if he don't takes the challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou risk Renown penalties for getting into duels with foes too much weaker than them. &quot;This challenge is beneath me, screw off,&quot; is baked into their thinking about these things.<br /> <br /> Also, is there a particular reason we're not trying to work some sort of base-line edition assumptions here? There's just so many combat rules, and supernatural powers, that have been adjusted over time, I'm not sure how you're going to figure anything out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess there is no official rule conversion for Fighting Style merits? </div> </div> </div>There's no official rules from conversion for anything from the WoD to the CofD and vice versa. There were a few stabs at some rough guidelines, but ultimately the systems are just too different for a lot of the more detail things.<br /> <br /> Also the WoD has equivalent mechanics to Fighting Style Merits in the Martial Arts Skill that's present in some of the books. Martial Arts is Brawl+ with extra moves Brawl users can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T15:25:46-07:00","id":1512640,"title":"","content":"This feels like utter silliness. When you cram so much extraordinary shit into one person they're no longer human for any real intents or purposes. And how in the hell are can you justify using things from multiple different mechanical systems to justify this.<br /> <br /> If you want a badass human NPC that can challenge the PC's, just go for it. But the whole mental exercise seems like a poorly thought out kitchenshink as it stands here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T17:33:59-07:00","id":1512659,"title":"","content":"I mean, it can be illustrative to look at how big the gap is, or if there isn't a hard gap how big is the grey area where the max-human can win in? 1 in a million? 1 in a thousand?<br /> <br /> But I reiterate that the only way to learn anything from these sorts of exercises is to pause reaching out all over the *oD games for edge cases to toss in, and start with some actual foundations to build anything else on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T02:23:18-07:00","id":1512699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I reiterate that the only way to learn anything from these sorts of exercises is to pause reaching out all over the *oD games for edge cases to toss in, and start with some actual foundations to build anything else on. </div> </div> </div>I always thought that essentially there was only Old World of Darkness and New World of Darkness. Are the rules so different in the various editions?<br /> <br /> Anyhow, what rules would you use in your game, most of times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T02:36:59-07:00","id":1512702,"title":"","content":"There are five editions of the WoD, and two editions of the CofD (when Paradox decided to return to the old WoD as their core product, the new WoD was renamed to the Chronicles of Darkness to reduce brand confusion keeping in mind that 'old' and 'new' are fan labels, not official ones). <br /> <br /> None of them are 100% compatible with each other. The WoD is notorious for not even being consistent between game-lines (the Dark Ages games for Revised and 20th being the largest deviations). For example, in some of the WoD games, flanking bonuses are dice bonuses, and in others they're difficulty bonuses. In combat, as a relatively mechanically intense part of the games, what are generally minor differences start to compound the most as more mechanical complexity increases.<br /> <br /> I personally default to the 20th base rules for the games that got them, or the Revised rules for the games that didn't, when it comes to the WoD, and the 2e rules for CofD. But there's not inherently correct answer for what you're trying to do, you just need to settle somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T04:22:14-07:00","id":1512708,"title":"","content":"And even within one generation of the WOD the rules different games are not identical, in V20 the difficulty for an attack is allways 6, in W20 and M20 it depends on the weapon you are using and varies between 4 and 8, and I think there also some differences when it comes to combat manoeuvrers,even between V20 and DAV20 there are difference in the rules.<br /> And there are a lot of other difference for example what what abilities exist, and Merits and Flaws tend tend also to have slightly different rules ans cost between the different games.<br /> <br /> I think the only exception to this are afaik the revised Dark Age books, where they used the same base rules for all games.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 05-25-2023, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T04:39:23-07:00","id":1512710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512702#post1512702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are five editions of the WoD, and two editions of the CofD (when Paradox decided to return to the old WoD as their core product, the new WoD was renamed to the Chronicles of Darkness to reduce brand confusion keeping in mind that 'old' and 'new' are fan labels, not official ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are actually even more editions.<br /> <br /> Even if we Ignore V5 (which is s completely new rules system) you have for Vampire alone, 4 editions of Masquerade and 3 Editions of Dark Age all with slightly different combat rules.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T11:15:44-07:00","id":1512754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512710#post1512710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are actually even more editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we are in general agreement here, by technical definition, there aren't. Vampire: the Dark Ages and it's supplements are part of 2nd Edition, Dark Ages: [Game] and supplements are part of the Revised edition, and Dark Ages: Vampire 20th Anniversary is... part of the 20th Anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> The fact that the later two aren't even compatible with the modern nights base Masquerade cores of the same edition is the problem at hand. They consciously chose not to make Vampire the Masquerade Revised and Dark Ages: Vampire Revised no follow the same rules. That's why the thread needs to start hashing things out more clearly about how to judge material for inclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T12:17:25-07:00","id":1512762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512754#post1512754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the later two aren't even compatible with the modern nights base Masquerade cores of the same edition is the problem at hand. They consciously chose not to make Vampire the Masquerade Revised and Dark Ages: Vampire Revised no follow the same rules. That's why the thread needs to start hashing things out more clearly about how to judge material for inclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that actually all 3 Dark Age edditions differ from the modern books of the same edition, the only the Victorian Age book uses the rules of the modern version.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T14:03:07-07:00","id":1512770,"title":"","content":"The 2e version does differ, but less drastically. It's more minor variants on Discipline powers, Roads vs. Paths, and a few mechanical things (most of which are standard 2e in other WoD games, or became standard in VtM Rev). DA Rev and DAV20 have changes to major systems like how multiple actions work,how armor works, some significant changes to Disciplines (esp. Celerity) and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:24:01-07:00","id":1512798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly#post1512416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little homebrew: a mortal character ( no ghoul, no sorcery, no infernal investments ) trained to the human limit in several martial arts ( Combat Styles from Armory Reloaded, transposed in the Old World of Darkness ruleset ).<br /> If I remember well there was a rule for extra use of Willpower in the book Mirrors. I've to research it.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, the question is: without going into the blatantly supernatural, can the strongest human take on a truly powerful supernatural being?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> So far:<br /> <br /> Strength ( heavy blows ) 5<br /> Dexterity ( close combat ) 5<br /> <br /> Dodge ( one-on-one ) 5<br /> Brawl ( boxing ) 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> * Ability aptitude - dodge<br /> * Ability aptitude - brawl<br /> * Berserker ( V20 Black Hand )<br /> <br /> Flaws:<br /> * Stress Atavism ( Guide to the Technocracy )</div> </div> </div> </div>my table used to have a house rule we used for this kind of stuff, basically it started to apply some old true-faith homebrew stuff we had just from the single minded belief in whatever. things like for e a body builder that regularly competed in and won weight lifting competitions would get a few dots in true-faith in themselves, 1 dot working like potence allowing them to channel their faith into superhuman strength levels, 2 dots granting access to armor of faith which lets them soak aggravated damage using their true-faith score + stam rating, so on and so forth. it made it much easier to keep your basically regular street level human as a possible threat depending on if they have &quot;true-faith&quot; in themselves, think like debo from friday all of a sudden hulking out and running your garou's pockets lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T20:36:04-07:00","id":1512815,"title":"","content":"So, your mortal-character, with a strength of five looks like Arnold-Schwarzenegger wished he could be back in the '80's and a Dex. of five, means he moves faster than Steven Seagal when he's attacking John Leguizamo.<br /> <br /> Any supernatural can be brought down by anyone or thing, given the right circumstances. Elder Vampires don't do well at high-noon and Lupines don't like silver brass-knuckles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T23:05:27-07:00","id":1512824,"title":"","content":"From a kit-bashing perspective, there are a couple of good think you are missing:<br /> 1) Good right hook (1pt) +2 damage dice to brawl attack (Demon the fallen player guide)<br /> 2) Natural aptitude (3 pts) pays a new level in the selected ability as they are one level lower and get an additional dice for any roll involving that ability (Demon the fallen player guide)<br /> 3) Graceful (2pts) -1 to any Dexterity-based action and botches does not embrace yourself (Sorcers Crusade)<br /> 4) Tough as nails (3pts) -1 to all soak rolls. (DA Inquisitor Companion)<br /> 5) Sturdy (4pts) + 1 bruised health level (V20 Dark age)<br /> 6) In the V20 DA tome of secrets there is a new background called martial training that provides new combat manoeuvres for brawl and melee, they usually increase the roll difficulties and provide circumstantial benefits. There are few manoeuvres but storytellers are encouraged to create new ones, maybe using other &quot;martial arts rules&quot; as guidelines (see below)<br /> 7) If I remember correctly, in the V20 DA tome of secrets there is a group of Cainites hunter called &quot;The Warriors of Dazbog&quot; that enjoy a significant reduction in the difficult penalty (-2 to the difficult ) for staking or beading a vampire.<br /> 8) There are multiple books that provide additional rules for martial arts as abilities with specific manoeuvre (Kindred of the East and its compendium, Demon Hunter X, M20), some of them are really useful for your aims such as the ones that allow you to inflict lethal damage with barehand attacks, you may take the relevant abilities and modify your character or you may convert them to the martial training background<br /> 9) You should also consider abilities like blind fighting that reduce combat-related penalties since vampires and werewolves could reduce their penalties for fighting in the dark.<br /> 10) In the Hunter book line there are a couple of useful abilities and backgrounds (Berserk, Iron willed, Grace under pressure,) that help with the initiative roll or increase the effective strength of the character but you may consider some of them &quot;supernatural&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem with kit-bashing is that the underlying rule system is not truly compatible and probably you are making something extremely unbalanced that defies the original premise &quot;Without going into the blatantly supernatural, can the strongest human take on a truly powerful supernatural being?&quot; because such character will be blatantly supernatural (Berserk, stress atavisms, etc.etc.).<br /> <br /> I think you need to fix some boundary conditions and then restart with your mental experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T00:03:51-07:00","id":1512829,"title":"","content":"Also potetally usefull.<ul><li>Charmed Existence (5 pts, Vampire Playersguide 2ndE): ignore one 1 on every roll</li> <li>Vindectiv (3 pts, Libellus Sanguinis I): +1 dice to all comabt pools when fighting one speific type of enemy</li> <li>True Berserk (5 pts, Wolfs of the See): Str+2, Sta+2, 3 additinal health levels, and a limited pain resitance\u200b</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T09:40:03-07:00","id":1512883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512815#post1512815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, your mortal-character, with a strength of five looks like Arnold-Schwarzenegger wished he could be back in the '80's and a Dex. of five, means he moves faster than Steven Seagal when he's attacking John Leguizamo.<br /> <br /> Any supernatural can be brought down by anyone or thing, given the right circumstances. Elder Vampires don't do well at high-noon and Lupines don't like silver brass-knuckles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hypertrophy =/= strength. your strength <i>potential </i>goes up with big muscles but you can be both more powerful and smaller than someone. Bodybuilders getting strong is a side effect of what they're doing; their main goal is to look big and/or beautiful (or at least impressive) if you look at competitive weight lifters, they've got completely different physiques and can often be small. There's a lot of neurological elements to strength that don't really translate as size. <br /> <br /> Which reminds me<br /> It's really, really difficult to get super strong while not compromising agility. 4/5/5? Achievable. Though I must complain internally because &quot;Stamina&quot; in WoD covers your ability to take a hit (being big is great) with your ability to exert yourself for a long time (being big is terrible) But pinnacle of strength types actually worsen their agility. Being really big is not great for your speed or range of motion, for example benchpress can reduce your shoulder's range of motion if you don't counter train, and IIRC sometimes neurological adaptations only apply to specific moves you train in. <br /> <br /> IDK, strength is a weird stat to put into a 1-5 perspective since there's a lot of quantifiable variance in it. \u017dydr\u016bnas Savickas might be the greatest strength athlete of all time but I think he'd be below average in any kind of climbing competition. But even if we don't get into specialist extremes there's still stuff like testosterone being a hell of a drug and men having a fantastic advantage over women in strength. When you're playing vampires, it doesn't matter; a 30kg girl can tear a bear in two with her bare hands like it's nothing, but with mortals it's a little strange. Women IRL are cautious with men because of that disparity, but when they both get averaged to 2 dots of strength.. I suppose there are difficulties if you wanna get simulations. Anyhow, I've digressed wildly. <br /> <br /> Maybe a mortal mass monster might really get an advantage over a lightweight master vampire. Weight goes into power. There unfortunately aren't any existing merits for extreme physiques beyond huge size, which really reads more like 'the embrace caused you to grow' rather than something within the realms of human transformation. <br /> <br /> A quick fun draft:<br /> <b>Hypertrophy (variable merit) </b><br /> You have exceptionally big and bulging muscles, . At storyteller's discretion, this may influence your intimidation pool. <br /> <br /> <b>2 points</b><br /> You have an extra bruised level. You gain one die to brawl damage and any action where your weight can be an advantage, but lose a die when it would be a disadvantage, such as climbing <br /> <br /> <b>5 points</b><br /> As the two point merit, but You have an additional extra bruised level. Your generational maximum for strength and stamina is 1 higher, your starting dexterity is limited to 1 and it takes twice as much XP to improve, your generational maximum for dexterity is one level lower. In addition, your heart is enlarged; the difficulty to target your heart is reduced by 1. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lightweight</b> (0 point merit) <br /> You are exceptionally lean in muscle tissue. Gain 1 die to all physical activities that take advantage of this, such as climbing, jumping, dodging, or running long distances. lose one die for anything where weight is useful, such as grappling, escaping a grapple, staying standing after a tackle, pushing, and so forth. Also lose 1 die from all ordinary unarmed damage, not including Feral Claws and it's like. <br /> <br /> <b>Ultralightweight </b> (1 point merit for vampires) <br /> While being emaciated might be devestating for mortals, it has it's advantages for vampires, especially in that they may increase their strength irrespective of the muscles they were embraced with. Lose one bruised level, double the dice pool gains and losses of lightweight. The Vampire can jump twice as high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T10:02:34-07:00","id":1512887,"title":"","content":"From personal experience. I train alone, bench pressing and free weights ( and push ups... sometimes ). I can tell you, increasing muscular mass is the hardest thing to achieve. To gain even a single pound of muscle ( not water, not fat: true muscle ) you must work really, really hard and it's inevitable to become stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T19:02:02-07:00","id":1514072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512887#post1512887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From personal experience. I train alone, bench pressing and free weights ( and push ups... sometimes ). I can tell you, increasing muscular mass is the hardest thing to achieve. To gain even a single pound of muscle ( not water, not fat: true muscle ) you must work really, really hard and it's inevitable to become stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can attest to that; I've worked a moving company, back in the day, lifted refrigerators and armoires up three-flights of stairs, in 90-degree heat, in the summer and I didn't gain a lot muscle-mass, per se, but I did look a little cut. But the best thing was, is that I could easily do it again and again with no soreness or pain the next day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T06:24:35-07:00","id":1514459,"title":"","content":"Even withouth taking in account the differences between editions, the answer is no.<br /> <br /> The strongest human would have an hard time with a <b><u>normal </u></b>supernatural. Any Brujah, Gangrel or Nosferatu Neonate are far more powerful than the best human can be. Discipline +dice from blood and there is simply no nothing to do. Let alone mental powers, thaumaturgy or eldritch shit like Vicissitude and Obtenebration.<br /> And Elders are totally on another level, event if we take in account &quot;weak&quot; young elders, like Calebros or Pieterzoon.<br /> Same goes for Crinos. A normal Crinos has a good shot at taking down an Elder Vampire. A mere human would die in the first to second turn of combat, no matter how min maxed.<br /> This for anything related to Old world of Darkness<br /> For the the New World of Darkness this is even truer, since supernaturals powers are stronger in that setting.<br /> It's simply not possible for a normal human to kill a Crinos, that's why against normal humans Crinos use by default &quot;Down and Dirty combat&quot;, because the combat is...purely aestethic.<br /> <br /> If you fight against supernaturals you must use their atavic weakness, play smart, and go in numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 06-10-2023, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T09:32:30-07:00","id":1514471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1512887#post1512887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From personal experience. I train alone, bench pressing and free weights ( and push ups... sometimes ). I can tell you, increasing muscular mass is the hardest thing to achieve. To gain even a single pound of muscle ( not water, not fat: true muscle ) you must work really, really hard and it's inevitable to become stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur you have to have really disciplined eating and work out habits to look like those men &amp; women on those fitness magazines. I started taking better care of myself by eating better and doing lots of cycling and doing basic pushups and modest weight lifting at work as I didn't like the way I was starting to look in my mid twenties. But I'd don't have the look for the muscle mags and I don't have that type of drive that they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:13:03-07:00","id":1514509,"title":"","content":"Remember that the &quot;drive&quot; is to get paid money to put your body through a lot of short term gain, long term harm, so you can be a model for as long as your body can take it, and digital artists can cover up some &quot;flaws.&quot; Muscle mags are just the male-oriented side of the business of selling impossible ideals of body image to get people to buy products they don't need instead of investing in real healthy life style choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T01:51:50-07:00","id":1514558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514459#post1514459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The strongest human would have an hard time with a <b><u>normal </u></b>supernatural. Any Brujah, Gangrel or Nosferatu Neonate are far more powerful than the best human can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that an average neonate is that strong. I mean just grab any book with NSC Templates (for V20 I think Anarch Unbound is the only one) and look at that stats of the least experienced ones, those are not particularly impressive.<br /> <br /> Most neonates will be only be able to spend on point of blood per turn, meaning the would need multiple turn and a lot of blood points to get to where the best human fighter could be.<br /> <br /> Most neonates are not going to be skilled fighters, and will only have a handfull of discipline points (and are not going to have particularly large pools when using these powers).<br /> <br /> A maxed out human fighter, would be a pretty tough opponent for a average neonate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T02:32:20-07:00","id":1514561,"title":"","content":"I'm taking the ready made &quot;physical&quot; characters that you can find in the various Clanbooks revised.<br /> These are starting characters, for session 1.<br /> <br /> Brujah Clanbook revised<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Paladin<br /> <br /> Generation 11<br /> STR 4,DEX 2,STAM 4<br /> <br /> BRAWL 2, DODGE 2<br /> <br /> CELERITY 2,POTENCE 2, PRESENCE 1<br /> <br /> WP 3&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Pugilist<br /> Generation 11<br /> <br /> STR 4,DEX 2,STAM 4<br /> <br /> BRAWL 4,DODGE 3<br /> <br /> CELERITY 2,FORTITUDE 1,POTENCE 1<br /> <br /> WP 4&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Small Town Sheriff<br /> Generation 10<br /> <br /> STR 4,DEX 2,STAM 4<br /> <br /> Brawl 3,dodge 1<br /> <br /> Dominate 1,Potence 2,Presence 1<br /> <br /> WP 4 </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Anachronism<br /> Generation 9<br /> <br /> STR 4,DEX 3,STAM 4<br /> <br /> BRAWL 2,DODGE 2<br /> <br /> POTENCE 3<br /> WP5 </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T02:46:50-07:00","id":1514562,"title":"","content":"And I'm taking in account only physical characters because when mental and eldritch disciplines are taken in account, there is simply no fight. Willpower will protect you from Dominate, but not from Serpentis, , Thaumaturgy, Vicissitude, Obtenebration or Quietus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 06-11-2023, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T04:18:07-07:00","id":1514566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514561#post1514561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm taking the ready made &quot;physical&quot; characters that you can find in the various Clanbooks revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those Characters have Pools of 5-6 dice in their Brawl pools, while the &quot;Super Trained Human&quot; would have Brawl and dodge Pools of 10.<br /> <br /> That would make him pretty hard to beat for anyone without Celerity. With Celerity it depends on what Edition you are using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514561#post1514561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower will protect you from Dominate, but not from Serpentis, , Thaumaturgy, Vicissitude, Obtenebration or Quietus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think usually Neonates are not going to have more than second level powers.<br /> - For Serpentis 1 you need also Eye contact, not sure if the same rules as for Dominate apply for that, for the second level you have to hit the target.<br /> - With Thaumaturgy I'm not sure which level 1 or 2 power would actually help you in a fight.<br /> - Obtenebration 1 is going to reduce the stamina of the &quot;Super Trained Human&quot; by 1 that's not that massive, Obtenebration 2 is iirc also effecting the user (If you don't build around that)<br /> - Quietus 1 is not that help full in afight, Quietus 2 requires you to hit you opponent<br /> - Vicissitude 1 is again not usefull in a fight, and Vicissitude 2 requires you to sucessfully grapple you opponent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:03:29-07:00","id":1514619,"title":"","content":"OK, so here's the thing about the 10 dice pool human brawler:<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Using V20 rules, and being a bit generous with averages, and a 10 dice attack with Strength 5 that's bashing? Let's say they roll 5 successes (the vampire didn't take a defensive action, at all). That's 9 dice of damage, so let's say they get 5 successes again. That would get reduced to 2B damage dealt if the Vampire failed their soak roll completely.<br /> <br /> That's how little of a threat a maxed out human's punches mean to a vampire. No dodging or soak, no Disciplines, no blood spending, no nothing but being a vampire... and the best human fighter in the world is doing the high end of average just to deal two damage.<br /> <br /> That attack also means no defense, so our vampire is counter attacking - and humans don't halve bashing damage (or soak the aggravated damage that vampires can deal with bites) - against no defensive action either.<br /> <br /> While the stat blocks posted above seem to be relying on the Revised implementation of Disciplines, it's not a huge deal. The vampire's best strategy is to take the max-human's opening hit(s), maybe spend a blood to heal if they need it (though most likely they don't and can spend it on Str instead), and then grapple as a counter. Potence 2-3 w/blood easily makes up for the difference in dice pools, and the vampire can start agg-biting.<br /> <br /> So not min-maxed to high heaven, not using something you even need to spend a ton of freebies on to be able to do, no prepping before the fight to pump up your physicals to 6/6/6 and snacking on someone to top up; just a decent fighter with a supernatural edge completely overturning everything the maxed out human can do. It would be a pretty slow fight by WoD standards, but time is on the vampire's side here.<br /> <br /> A fairly combat oriented but hardly optimally so neonate... with huge potential to get way stronger... is absolutely the statistical favored to win against a human that's reached the max a human can reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:55:45-07:00","id":1514629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514619#post1514619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so here's the thing about the 10 dice pool human brawler:<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Using V20 rules, and being a bit generous with averages, and a 10 dice attack with Strength 5 that's bashing? Let's say they roll 5 successes (the vampire didn't take a defensive action, at all). That's 9 dice of damage, so let's say they get 5 successes again. That would get reduced to 2B damage dealt if the Vampire failed their soak roll completely.<br /> <br /> That's how little of a threat a maxed out human's punches mean to a vampire. No dodging or soak, no Disciplines, no blood spending, no nothing but being a vampire... and the best human fighter in the world is doing the high end of average just to deal two damage.<br /> <br /> That attack also means no defense, so our vampire is counter attacking - and humans don't halve bashing damage (or soak the aggravated damage that vampires can deal with bites) - against no defensive action either.<br /> <br /> While the stat blocks posted above seem to be relying on the Revised implementation of Disciplines, it's not a huge deal. The vampire's best strategy is to take the max-human's opening hit(s), maybe spend a blood to heal if they need it (though most likely they don't and can spend it on Str instead), and then grapple as a counter. Potence 2-3 w/blood easily makes up for the difference in dice pools, and the vampire can start agg-biting.<br /> <br /> So not min-maxed to high heaven, not using something you even need to spend a ton of freebies on to be able to do, no prepping before the fight to pump up your physicals to 6/6/6 and snacking on someone to top up; just a decent fighter with a supernatural edge completely overturning everything the maxed out human can do. It would be a pretty slow fight by WoD standards, but time is on the vampire's side here.<br /> <br /> A fairly combat oriented but hardly optimally so neonate... with huge potential to get way stronger... is absolutely the statistical favored to win against a human that's reached the max a human can reach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is even worse if you do the comparison with Garou. Not even an optimized Garou, some Rank 1 with tertiary Physical stats, just the stat increases + regeneration + soak + rage extra actions + claws is ahead of the world most optimized mortal fighter. If you start using just a couple of combat gifts? It becomes a massacre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-11-2023, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T22:45:08-07:00","id":1514653,"title":"","content":"The only viable - and I use the term <u><b>very loosely</b></u> - scenario where a super-trained human defeat a Garou or elder vampire barehandedly is from a surprise attack and tear its head off<br /> The force required to rip a person\u2019s head off is no different with one or two hands, but the manner of tearing the head off according to the weight and musculature of the subject will vary greatly by the operator who is facilitating this task. Obviously ripping requires a different expenditure of energy for each different subject, but from a specialists perspective, the manner and the person facilitating the task make the real difference. <br /> Nature tends to design structures that don\u2019t withstand torsion very well. However, if you\u2019re just talking about ripping a head completely off, studies about hanging loop briefly mentions a force of 5600 newtons as occasionally causing decapitations.<br /> Anyways, a boxers can exert up to 5,000 newtons of force per punch. Pulling is more difficult, as according to the Canadian Centre for Occupational Health and Safety, a worker supporting his or her body against a firm structure can develop horizontal pushing or pulling forces of up to 675 newtons...<br /> But in theory, if the stars are right in every Blue Moon... and stack all what you could AND manage to somehow sneakattack to grab and tear the opponent head of...?<br /> Ehh... <i>maaaaaaaaaaybe</i>?<br /> (And don't even think about ripping the heart out; even If you had enough power to shove your hand through the sternum and rib cage of the human body, you would first break every finger, smash every tendon and rip all the muscles in your hand and possibly every bone in your wrist before being able to seize the heart, losing your ability to grasp it. If you are going to ask for super strength, you also better ask for super endurance as well.)<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T03:53:40-07:00","id":1514676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514619#post1514619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how little of a threat a maxed out human's punches mean to a vampire. No dodging or soak, no Disciplines, no blood spending, no nothing but being a vampire... and the best human fighter in the world is doing the high end of average just to deal two damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok the Bashing damage is a problem, but if you had a human Sword Fighter with Stats like that, that would be a problem for most neonates.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T04:08:18-07:00","id":1514677,"title":"","content":"Not as much as you'd think?<br /> <br /> Melee neonate takes Dex 4 instead of Strength 4 and Celerity, then passive dice bonus and spending a blood on Dex to get their dice-pool to 11-12, and then uses parries. Mortal can't soak lethal, and steadily takes a bit of damage. By turn three the neonate can afford to use active Celerity and the maxed for melee human goes down.<br /> <br /> The chance for an upset certainly goes up, but the ability to soak lethal is still a huge advantage to off-set a bad roll or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:25:58-07:00","id":1514734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514619#post1514619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so here's the thing about the 10 dice pool human brawler:<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter..</div> </div> </div> </div>My knee-jerk reaction would be to argue against this because headshots + kicks/elbows having potential for more base damage + doing lethal but then I remember how RAW aimed shots and special moves have ridiculously high penalties that don't really represent reality <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:26:51-07:00","id":1514748,"title":"","content":"Also, &quot;reality&quot; is rather meaningless in a discussion about what happens when you punch a vampire.<br /> <br /> This is also the classic issue with White Room combat theories with rules that aren't meant to be fun in a White Room scenario. However the quality of special moves are written, the White Room devalues them because it takes away the reason to do &quot;special&quot; things. The White Room abhors high risk high reward strategies because it's the White Room. There isn't the reality to create moments for such tactics to be viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:20:17-07:00","id":1514828,"title":"","content":"Eh, short of something like fate or destiny, the presence of magic in a setting doesn't give you the excuse to write off the mundane. Questions like &quot;why is Samwell Tarly still so fat&quot; or &quot;How does the Witcher continent maintain it's london-like ethnic diversity after thousands of years&quot; don't become invalid because somewhere, miles away in that setting, there's a few dragons and some corpses became monsters. <br /> <br /> And it's a natural reaction to consider problems as things to solve. Oh, my gun barely leaves a dent in it, how much bigger does my next gun need to be, should I buy armour piercing rounds? Since prehistory, if something didn't go down when you hit it with a stick, you needed a bigger stick, or a sharper stick, or a rock, or metal. Just accept human nature and accept that if vampires or aliens or dragons or demons or whatever else is unknown suddenly became very real our monkey brains would delight in inventing stratagems to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:47:39-07:00","id":1514832,"title":"","content":"Hmm... true<br /> if Homosapiens are good at one thing, it\u2019s killing other things. We\u2019re so good at it that we\u2019ve made entire other species cease to exist without even trying...<br /> Clever monkeys always find a way to innovate...<br /> <br /> &quot;Because he rather liked people.<br /> It was a major failing in a demon.<br /> Oh, he did his best to make their short lives miserable, because that was his job, but nothing he could think up was half as bad as the stuff they thought up themselves. They seemed to have a talent for it. It was built into the design, somehow. They were born into a world that was against them in a thousand little ways, and then devoted most of their energies to making it worse. Over the years Crowley had found it increasingly difficult to find anything demonic to do which showed up against the natural background of generalized nastiness. There had been times, over the past millenium, when he'd felt like sending a message back Below saying, Look, we may as well give up right now, we might as well shut down Dis and Pandemonium and everywhere and move up here, there's nothing we can do to them that they don't do to themselves and they do things we've never even though of, often involving electrodes. They've got what we lack. They've got imagination. And electricity, of course.\u201d<br /> \u2015 Neil Gaiman Terry Pratchett, Good Omens: The Nice and Accurate Prophecies of Agnes Nutter, Witch<br /> <br /> But I think we a bit drifted from the original question: <b>Can a super-trained human defeat a Garou or elder vampire barehandedly?</b><br /> The answer is still: probably not - at least in my humble opinion<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T13:38:32-07:00","id":1514876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514828#post1514828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, short of something like fate or destiny, the presence of magic in a setting doesn't give you the excuse to write off the mundane. Questions like &quot;why is Samwell Tarly still so fat&quot; or &quot;How does the Witcher continent maintain it's london-like ethnic diversity after thousands of years&quot; don't become invalid because somewhere, miles away in that setting, there's a few dragons and some corpses became monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about &quot;there's a few dragons thousand of miles away.&quot; We're talking about walking up to the dragon and punching it in the face. Since dragons aren't real, what happens if you punch one is the realms of fiction, not mundane things.<br /> <br /> I'm writing of the mundane, because the mundane explicitly doesn't work in the scenario proposed in the setting being discussed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's a natural reaction to consider problems as things to solve. </div> </div> </div>OK. What was my first post to this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T19:15:37-07:00","id":1514908,"title":"","content":"If you want to be a superhuman trained fighter that can actually defeat dangerous occult beings, you're pretty much going to have to play a Shih from Demon Hunter X. Even highly trained agents from the other half of the book's Strike Force Zero are likely to end up about as successful as in the beginning comic (i.e. 60% mortality rate against a powerful fomor, a typical group of monsters from one of the major book lines is likely to utterly destroy a typical five agent unit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T02:45:29-07:00","id":1514930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514677#post1514677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Melee neonate takes Dex 4 instead of Strength 4 and Celerity, then passive dice bonus and spending a blood on Dex to get their dice-pool to 11-12, and then uses parries. Mortal can't soak lethal, and steadily takes a bit of damage. By turn three the neonate can afford to use active Celerity and the maxed for melee human goes down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends again a bit on the edition.<br /> With pre V20 rues where Celerity doesn't increase you Dex, an average neonate would need 5+ turns to the pools that high.<br /> <br /> I think the Edition most advantageous rules for the mortal would be Revised Dark Ages (Celerity doesn't give a Dex Bonus, and pools aren't split but only reduced by few dice for multiple actions), V20 would probably one of the worst options for the mortal (Celerity gives a Dex Bonus, pools are split).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:23:56-07:00","id":1514935,"title":"","content":"I had said I was using V20.<br /> <br /> DA Rev might make lethal damage melee a bit more in the maxed out mortal's favor, but it also skews other scenarios against them (like Potence being a passive +X successes boost.<br /> <br /> Of course, the best option for a melee vampire changes with the changes in Disciplines. The character that has Potence 2/Celerity 2 with Dex 4 just spams 3 attacks (DA: Rev means no cap on blood spent on Celerity actions). The mortal really doesn't have many tactical choices but to try to one-shot the vampire or toss a lot of dice and hope luck is on their side. Multiple action penalties rack up fast, so trying to mix up attacks and defenses runs a risk of just slowly accumulating Potence boosted attacks since the vampire is always attack full dice pool.<br /> <br /> If the mortal goes for a one-hit kill, it's a long shot because that means 7 damage after soak. If that does 6 damage or less the vampire spends a WP to ignore wound penalties and wins.<br /> <br /> If the mortal tries to use their larger base dice-pool to match 3 actions for 3 actions, their dice-pools go to near tied. Any hits are going to be 1 success ones, so no carry over damage, with the vampire retaining the advantages of Potence 2 and soaking the damage. The mortal dies on the 4th hit guaranteed, if not sooner.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that DA vampires start at lower generation, so they have more blood. I don't recall if DA Rev ever clarified, but IIRC the wording on Celerity says that blood spent on extra actions doesn't count towards your cap, so that also means the can blow blood on Dex buffing and healing too; and getting to 2/bp a turn doesn't require maxing your Generation background so that would be a consideration as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T05:59:04-07:00","id":1514948,"title":"","content":"In DA means the Gen is one lower as in modern, and as long as that doesn't bring the neonate to 9th Gen the differnce isn't that major.<br /> <br /> And I'm really more assuming an average Neonate not one that is maxed out for Combat.<br /> <br /> Might be that this fight is still in favour of the vampire, but not so much that the human would just be steam rolled, and it would likely really come down to the dice.<br /> And if the Human has like the OP suggested some of the more powerfull merits (Ability aptitude, Berserker, Well Marked ...) that would give him imo the edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T08:57:38-07:00","id":1514963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1514948#post1514948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In DA means the Gen is one lower as in modern, and as long as that doesn't bring the neonate to 9th Gen the differnce isn't that major.<br /> <br /> <b>And I'm really more assuming an average Neonate not one that is maxed out for Combat.</b><br /> <br /> Might be that this fight is still in favour of the vampire, but not so much that the human would just be steam rolled, and it would likely really come down to the dice.<br /> And if the Human has like the OP suggested some of the more powerfull merits (Ability aptitude, Berserker, Well Marked ...) that would give him imo the edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even IF the average neonate does not have Combat disciplines, other options would kill the world best mortal fighter.<br /> <br /> For example, someone with Dominate or Presence 3 would stop the mortal easily.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Put in another way, it is the world best fighter vs a supernaturally enhanced person. It was never meant to be a &quot;fair&quot; fight, it can not be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:15:42-07:00","id":1515017,"title":"","content":"Um, I haven't been using &quot;maxed out for combat&quot; neonates in the slightest. I've been using the stat blocks Undead Rabbit posted, maybe with some shifting of dots around like flipping the listed Strength and Dexterity, or Brawl to Melee.<br /> <br /> Edit: As well, more min-maxed neonates just stuck with using vampire rules feels plenty fair if the maxed out mortal is picking and choosing Merits/etc. from four editions and any game line as long as they're not overtly supernatural ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-14-2023, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:31:30-07:00","id":1515020,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5199\" data-vbnamecard=\"5199\">Aahz</a> white room scenarios will fail because it becomes a full frontal set of attacks, and those are DEADLY coming from Vampires or Garou.<br /> <br /> If you want to make it more believable, ala Predator 1 film: Predator vs &quot;Dutch&quot;, still the advantages are overwhelmingly in favour of the supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To make it simple, post your desired stats, both for the human and the Vampire / Garou and pick the location/circumstances; we will use the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OK1pf7N3tIoPYYhX0kL37s-awQ0owwKNZlopwZ4EjHI/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">OWOD probability calculator</a>\u200b to see the likelihood of success and see if that suffices.<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, I am getting the impression you are being contrarian for the sake of being contrarian. IMHO enough posters have shown with many arguments and clarity why the mortal can not win, yet you insist on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:53:34-07:00","id":1515022,"title":"","content":"I would also ask to stick to one edition, and one game-line for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:29:32-07:00","id":1515066,"title":"","content":"Small inclusion. W20.<br /> 1. Werewolves are pack creatures. Human npc would probably confront entire pack = quick death.<br /> 2. With low level gift - spirit of the fray - garou will be first with massive boost of dices from crinos. If your pc is maximized why Ahroun couldn't be? Why he couldn't have 4-5 dots in dexterity and strength. With bigger dice poool he'll have more chances to hit. You need armor to soak, but it will lower your dex so dodging is harder. With wind claws your armor is useless.<br /> 3. Does human character have silver?<br /> 4. Werewolf can jump out from umbra suprising oponent.<br /> 5. Luna's armor.<br /> 6. Or theurg can summon something that npc is not ready for, for example electricity elemental.<br /> <br /> I've been running something like that years ago, when in official adventure pc are confronting guards (silver ammo packed guns, delirium resistant fomori) with almost maximized stats. First rank Silver Fang ahroun tore through them in two - three rounds.<br /> <br /> Vampire?<br /> Nosferatu. He don't need to be combatant. Let's put points in stealth, dex and firearms. <br /> 1. Animalism - simple rat will show me where your pc is.<br /> 2. Stealth is the key to get as close as possible or use unseen presence.<br /> 3. Make point blank headshot. Game over.<br /> <br /> Thing is that human is maximized so why other are not? Even if they are fresh characters, they still have huge arsenal of possibilities to ged rid of this human.<br /> End of inclusion.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T02:35:01-07:00","id":1515077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1512416-can-a-super-trained-human-defeat-a-garou-or-elder-vampire-barehandedly?p=1515017#post1515017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, I haven't been using &quot;maxed out for combat&quot; neonates in the slightest. I've been using the stat blocks Undead Rabbit posted, maybe with some shifting of dots around like flipping the listed Strength and Dexterity, or Brawl to Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>4 Physical Disciplines and Physical Attributes primary is at least pretty combat centric.<br /> <br /> But I think in the end it really depends on what Edition you use, and how you define Average Neonate. And at least the Pre Gens and NPCs from the official sources had often pretty terrible stats.<br /> <br /> I mean the ones Undead Rabbit posted have Willpower scores between 3-5...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 06-15-2023, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:20:14-07:00","id":1515085,"title":"","content":"lbeaumanior already laid out the ask of you to set some parameters if you're not happy with the ones on the table.<br /> <br /> As I felt I already made the case, editions only really impact what strategies are best for supernaturals to compensate with having lower dice-pools before they apply innate or bough powers. You're not going to hobble the supernatural by changing editions, you're just going to change what the effective things to take are.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the pre-gens usually have shitty stats... but at the same time they're still winning these hypotheticals (or at least winning more often than not by a serious margin). The whole point of using them is there's no such thing as &quot;average neonate&quot; and picking their sub-par stats for combat focused characters compared to what you could start with is at least a functional starting point.<br /> <br /> Are you actually trying to get at a point here? Because I've done examples in two different editions, and I feel like I've done plenty to illustrate that, generally speaking, being a supernatural with some combat buffs &gt; being a mortal with really high stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}